\b0\fs24 \cf7 Banana Pancake Trail
\b\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6\sb100\sa100\partightenfactor0

\b0\fs24 \cf7 The tired travelling or backpacking route across the Southeast Asian peninsula \'97 Thailand, Cambodia, Laos, and Vietnam \'97 is known in the travel world as the Banana Pancake Trail, so called for the many stalls selling banana pancakes that are widely sold in the cities along the trail. This route is popular for a reason. It\'92s exotic, \'93tourist-friendly\'94, and most importantly, cheap, the qualities that make a destination perfect for both seasoned and newbie backpackers, especially those traveling alone. \
Head for the Banana Pancake Trail to have your solo backpacking debut. It is one of the most unforgettable trips to date. For a backpacker, although the region looks, tastes, and sounds different, it still fosters an atmosphere that made one feel like home. It is no surprise that travellers returned later that year, and every two years since.\
\pard\tx720\tx1099\pardeftab720\fi-360\ri-6\sb100\sa100\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\fs20 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\fs24 \cf7 Route 1: Singapore, Malacca, Kuala Lumpur, Langkawi, Penang, Cameron Highlands\
\pard\tx720\tx1099\pardeftab720\fi-360\ri-6\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f4\fs20 \cf7 {\listtext	
\f3 \cf0 \uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\fs24 \cf7 Route 2: Phuket, Krabi, Bangkok, Ayutthaya, Siem Reap, Ho Chi Minh City, Phan Thiet, Mui Ne\
\pard\tx720\tx1099\pardeftab720\fi-360\ri-6\sb100\sa100\partightenfactor0
\cf7 In this ASEAN TRAVEL GUIDE, we\'92ll be sharing with you how we plan our travel or backpacking trips across Southeast Asia. We will start off with 2 sample routes.\
